  "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 170, Number 130 (Tuesday, August 13, 2024)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"https://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Ms. PORTER:\nH.R. 9354.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle I, Section 8 of the U.S. Constitution\nThe single subject of this legislation is:\nTo amend the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 to make certain\ntemporary provisions relating to the child tax credit\npermanent, to make such credit fully refundable, and to\nincrease the corporate tax rate.\n[Page H4991]\n</pre>",
